From 52a68a95ae78c6094c42f7d4225386cfa4fff063 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:17:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Format values with picture clauses, and validate them

Values were shown as stored: 1234.5 instead of $1,234.50, 123456789
instead of 123 456 789. Picture clauses are used by most fields of tax
and immigration forms.

Numeric, date and text picture clauses now format values for display
(<format>) and editing (<ui>), and parse what is typed back into the
stored value. Values that do not fit a picture show as they are, as do
those of comb fields and of fields too short for the formatted text.

Validation now follows <validate>: values must fit its picture clause,
validate scripts that evaluate to false fail, and execValidate() also
checks required fields. After an edit, the first failure is reported
with the form's message for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
